{"step_index":68,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T18:06:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-15T23:36:35+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-15T23:36:45+05:30\nThe search for \"\"Nitish Rajput\" YouTube animation software tools production how videos are made behind the scenes\" returned the following summary:\nNitish Rajput’s documentary-style videos are widely recognized for their high-quality production, engaging storytelling, and sophisticated motion graphics[1]. While the specific internal workflow of his team is proprietary, many professional editors have reverse-engineered his style, identifying the core tools and techniques used to achieve his signature look[2][3][4].\n\n### Core Software & Tools\nThe \"Nitish Rajput style\" is primarily built on a foundation of professional motion design and non-linear editing software:\n\n*   **Adobe After Effects:** This is the primary tool for his complex animations[3][5]. It is used to create:\n    *   **3D Camera Movements:** Establishing depth and parallax effects to make static images or text feel cinematic[2][3][6].\n    *   **Map Animations:** Often utilizing plugins like **GeoLayers 3** to create detailed, animated geographical maps[1][7].\n    *   **Motion Graphics:** Creating custom lower-thirds, timeline animations, and dynamic number counters[2][8][9].\n*   **Adobe Premiere Pro:** Typically used for the main video editing, including the \"assembly\" of the story, pacing, syncing voiceovers with B-roll, and final color grading[10][3][5].\n*   **Adobe Photoshop:** Used extensively for preparing assets, such as isolating subjects from backgrounds (cutouts), creating photo collages, and designing textures[2][3][11].\n*   **Other Tools:** Creators often use platforms like **ElevenLabs** for high-quality voiceovers (if applicable), **Envato Elements** or **Freepik** for stock footage and assets, and various audio production tools for sound design[3][4].\n\n### Behind-the-Scenes Production Process\nThe production of his documentary-style videos generally follows a structured \"high-retention\" workflow[4][5]:\n\n1.  **Storytelling & Scripting:** The process begins with a strong, research-heavy narrative designed to hook the audience from the start[10][3][5].\n2.  **Asset Preparation:** Before animation, images and documents are processed in Photoshop to create \"cutouts\" or layered files that can be animated in 3D space[2][3].\n3.  **Animation & Compositing:** In After Effects, these layers are placed in 3D space. By manipulating a virtual camera, editors create the \"parallax\" effect—where foreground and background elements move at different speeds, adding a sense of 3D depth to 2D images[2][12][6].\n4.  **Pacing & Sound Design:** A critical component is the use of subtle sound effects (SFX) like paper rustling, ink reveals, or camera \"clicks\" to accompany transitions[13][14]. This, combined with tight cuts and strategic music placement, maintains viewer retention throughout the video[10][8][5].\n5.  **Color Grading:** A final pass is often applied to give the video a cohesive, often \"dark\" or \"investigative\" cinematic tone[13][15].\n\nIf you are looking to learn these techniques, many creators publish \"breakdown\" tutorials specifically labeled as \"Nitish Rajput style\" that provide project files and step-by-step guidance on mastering the After Effects graph editor and camera animation[2][8][6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [ezedit.in](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHyaLBjyqoV-RHzcNyZvLUQyIiQfs29zwpeoB2lzyfwhLCm83Y3A_NPI-iOnkMxJw5bIFjCxkprQDcv9MBxIscv9ztlhcnY3kmfKsiXi632KBoxhHZsJ8_RVMpNQAgzzQB7OGAsZfQudqlVDcgM0uReMaBtaWikfhUMsHsl5PiO38K6m0EQZRVOr6g7Z4XxP2jTec5YPKrXtKATBikxQbw=)\n[2] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH0wAhwwNvnm6fgL_h1f28mRL27sySSJ0xqUybhko_dluX_JlfNP76YiKwdLQlHw8LYqDZiv_Rooq2Eq14RB1CBwVv6WPjyiHfMJLe5o3TPZcYKhLIlmknoP-XBgR5P72k=)\n[3] [facebook